WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.867 --> 00:00:07.718
Once upon a time, there lived a man.

2
00:00:07.719 --> 00:00:09.780
The man was a miser.

3
00:00:09.781 --> 00:00:14.208
He loved gold, but he hated to spend it.

4
00:00:14.209 --> 00:00:18.870
One day, the miser decided to bury all his gold.

5
00:00:18.871 --> 00:00:21.283
He dug a hole in his garden.

6
00:00:21.284 --> 00:00:26.575
Then he carefully put his gold into the hole.

7
00:00:26.576 --> 00:00:31.479
"You are all mine!" the miser said to his gold.

8
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.553
"No one knows where you are, except me!"

9
00:00:34.554 --> 00:00:41.385
The miser laughed and did a funny dance.

10
00:00:41.386 --> 00:00:45.374
Every day, the miser went into his garden.

11
00:00:45.375 --> 00:00:47.282
He dug up his hole.

12
00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:50.136
The miser wanted to see his gold.

13
00:00:50.137 --> 00:00:54.020
He wanted to touch it.

14
00:00:54.021 --> 00:00:57.276
Each time the miser said the same thing.

15
00:00:57.277 --> 00:01:00.438
"No one knows where you are, except me!"

16
00:01:00.439 --> 00:01:06.823
Then he laughed and did a funny dance.

17
00:01:06.824 --> 00:01:11.366
One day, a man was passing by the miser's garden.

18
00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:14.265
He heard the miser laughing loudly.

19
00:01:14.266 --> 00:01:19.169
"Why is that miser so happy?" the man asked himself.

20
00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:24.167
The man looked over the fence.

21
00:01:24.168 --> 00:01:27.110
He saw the miser hide his gold.

22
00:01:27.111 --> 00:01:31.266
"I know where your gold is too!" the man said.

23
00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:36.009
He rubbed his hands together greedily.

24
00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:39.241
Later that night, the man returned.

25
00:01:39.242 --> 00:01:41.250
He was wearing a mask.

26
00:01:41.251 --> 00:01:44.215
He came to take the miser's gold.

27
00:01:44.216 --> 00:01:48.089
Yes, that man was a robber.

28
00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:52.567
The next day, the miser went to look at his gold again.

29
00:01:52.568 --> 00:01:55.790
He dug and dug, but found nothing.

30
00:01:55.791 --> 00:02:00.472
"What? No! This cannot be!" shouted the miser.

31
00:02:00.473 --> 00:02:02.323
The hole was empty.

32
00:02:02.324 --> 00:02:07.391
His gold was gone.

33
00:02:07.392 --> 00:02:10.449
Some people heard the miser shouting.

34
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:14.111
"What happened?" asked one old woman.

35
00:02:14.112 --> 00:02:21.052
"My gold! Someone took my gold!" cried the miser.

36
00:02:21.053 --> 00:02:24.932
"Where was your gold?" asked the woman.

37
00:02:24.933 --> 00:02:29.203
The miser explained how he buried his gold in the garden.

38
00:02:29.204 --> 00:02:36.524
He also told them he used to come and look at his gold every day.

39
00:02:36.525 --> 00:02:39.984
The village people shook their heads quietly.

40
00:02:39.985 --> 00:02:42.657
They knew the man was a miser.

41
00:02:42.658 --> 00:02:45.040
"Did you ever take any of it out?"

42
00:02:45.041 --> 00:02:47.199
asked a man wearing a hat.

43
00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:52.773
"No, I only came to look at it!" answered the miser.

44
00:02:52.774 --> 00:02:57.988
"Then you can come and look at this empty hole every day," the man said.

45
00:02:57.989 --> 00:03:04.454
"If you don't spend your riches, it is the same as having no riches at all!"
